  "note": "Annual election of three members of the Holywood Urban Council; nominations taken 2 January 1930 and no poll (Belfast News-Letter, 3 January 1930, p. 9). Only two nominations were received for three vacancies: the retiring members Morrison and M'Cavana were nominated, and Jonathan Jefferson, the third retiring member, was declared re-elected without nomination. Returned unopposed."
